Painting
Large-scale painting is not permitted in the exhibition centre. All exhibitors carrying out fabrication of their stand space need to neatly ﬁnish the backside up to the complete height of their display. No spray painting of any type is permitted in the exhibition halls. However, small scale "touch-up" painting of the exhibits and stands is permitted during the move-in period with all necessary safety precautions in place. These precautions include:
Painting in a properly ventilated area;
Use non-toxic, non-aerosol paints;
No painting near the exhibition centre's vertical structures (i.e. walls);
No washing of painting materials within or surrounding the exhibition centre.
All ﬂammable materials (such as thinners) are to be safely placed and removed from the hall immediately after use.
Spray painting and colours mixed with ﬂammable substances are strictly not permitted, both inside and outside the building.
